    "summary": "Traditional IRAs offer potential tax deductions now with taxable withdrawals in retirement, while Roth IRAs use after-tax contributions for tax-free growth and withdrawals. Choosing between them depends primarily on your current versus expected future tax bracket, income level, age, and retirement goals.",
